[exit 5]

$ jailops volume list
NAME     STORAGE   USED   SIZE        OWNER     MODE   ATTACHED TO       COMMENT
vault    default   0 B    5G          770:770   0700   vault (locked)    -
vault2   default   0 B    unlimited   0:0       0755   vault2 (locked)   -

$ jailops jail list
NAME     STATE    IMAGE               GEN   ADDRESSES    AUTOSTART   AGE
vault    locked   freebsd-15@stable   g1    10.20.0.10   -           3h
vault2   locked   freebsd-15@stable   g1    10.20.0.11   -           3h

$ jailops jail start vault
! locked: jail "vault" is locked: the encrypted volume(s) vault wait for a passphrase
! hint: jailops volume unlock vault
[exit 5]

$ jailops explain locked
locked

Cause:  An encrypted volume of the jail waits for its passphrase (after a host boot or a lock); a locked jail does not start.
Fix:    Run 'jailops volume unlock NAME' for the volume the error names (add --start to start the jail at once); a jail due for autostart starts after the unlock.
HTTP:   409
Exit:   5

$ jailops volume unlock vault
! bad_passphrase: the passphrase is not correct
! hint: Type the passphrase again. A forgotten passphrase cannot be recovered: the data of the volume is lost (docs/storage.md). (jailops explain bad_passphrase)
[exit 3]

$ jailops volume unlock vault --start
volume/vault unlocked and its jail started

